<section id="methodology" class="methodology">
	<h2>How the curation works</h2>
	<ol>
		<li>
			<strong>Collection.</strong> Scripts periodically search public
			sources (NASA, arXiv, ESA, JAXA, and others) for Moon-related
			content.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Draft.</strong> Every new item becomes a draft — never
			published automatically. Drafts live in a separate folder
			(<code>_drafts/</code>) and never appear on the site.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Human review.</strong> A draft only becomes a publication
			after someone reviews the summary, source attribution, and
			image/license credits.
		</li>
		<li>
			<strong>Mandatory attribution.</strong> Every published item has a
			source name, a link to the original material, and, when
			applicable, an image credit — we never reproduce the original
			content in full.
		</li>
	</ol>
	<p>
		This site's code and ingestion scripts are open; see
		<code>docs/study-notes/</code> in the repository for notes on each
		source.
	</p>
</section>

